  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree consisting of NNN nodes where the value of node iii is AiA_iAi​.\n\nYou are also given an **odd** integer K&nbsp;(1≤K&lt;N)K \\ (1 \\leq K \\lt N)K&nbsp;(1≤K&lt;N).\n\nYou can perform the following operation any (possibly zero) number of times:\n\n\nSelect an integer x&nbsp;(−109≤x≤109)x \\ (-10^9 \\leq x \\leq 10^9)x&nbsp;(−109≤x≤109) and two nodes iii and j&nbsp;(1≤i≤j≤N)j \\ (1 \\leq i \\leq j \\leq N)j&nbsp;(1≤i≤j≤N), such that dist(i,j)=Kdist(i,j)=Kdist(i,j)=K;\nAdd xxx to both AiA_iAi​ and AjA_jAj​.\nFind the **minimum** value of ∑i=1N∣Ai∣\\sum_{i=1}^{N} |A_i|∑i=1N​∣Ai​∣ you can get after performing any number of operations.\n\nNote that dist(i,j)dist(i,j)dist(i,j) denotes the number of edges in the shortest path between nodes iii and jjj.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains two positive integers NNN and KKK, the number of nodes and the required distance.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers, A1,A2…ANA_1, A_2 \\ldots A_NA1​,A2​…AN​ −-− denoting the array AAA.\nThe following next N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two integers uuu and vvv, denoting an edge between nodes uuu and vvv. It is guaranteed that the given edges form a tree.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the minimum sum that can be obtained.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤K&lt;N≤5⋅1051 \\leq K \\lt N \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^51≤K&lt;N≤5⋅105",
      "1≤u,v≤N1 \\leq u, v \\leq N1≤u,v≤N",
      "−109≤Ai≤109-10^9 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
