      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 1\n2 2\n1 2\n2 1\n0 -1\n1 2\n4 3\n1 -10 -10 1\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4",
        "output": "0\n1\n20",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: In one operation, select x=−2x = -2x=−2 and (i,j)=(1,2)(i,j) = (1,2)(i,j)=(1,2) where dist(1,2)=1dist(1, 2) = 1dist(1,2)=1.\nThus, we make A1=2−2=0A_1 = 2-2 = 0A1​=2−2=0 and A2=2−2=0A_2 = 2-2 = 0A2​=2−2=0.\nWe achieve the minimum possible value of ∑i=1N∣Ai∣=0\\sum_{i=1}^{N} |A_i| = 0∑i=1N​∣Ai​∣=0.\nTest case 222: Initially, ∑i=1N∣Ai∣=0+∣−1∣=1\\sum_{i=1}^{N} |A_i| = 0+|-1| = 1∑i=1N​∣Ai​∣=0+∣−1∣=1.\nIt can be shown that we cannot make the required value less than 111 in any number of operations.\nTest case 333: In one operation, choose x=−1x = -1x=−1 and (i,j)=(1,4)(i, j) = (1, 4)(i,j)=(1,4). Thus, A1=1−1=0A_1 = 1-1 = 0A1​=1−1=0 and A4=1−1=0A_4 = 1-1 = 0A4​=1−1=0.\nWe achieve the minimum possible value of ∑i=1N∣Ai∣=0+∣−10∣+∣−10∣+0=20\\sum_{i=1}^{N} |A_i| = 0+|-10|+|-10|+0 = 20∑i=1N​∣Ai​∣=0+∣−10∣+∣−10∣+0=20."
